From 9fd10b0d9207816a8e8f90b20523746b395a8c08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: naelolaiz <1333555+naelolaiz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 03:16:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] main/dtc: build pylibfdt with SWIG 4.5

SWIG 4.5 no longer defines PyInt_AsLong and PyString_FromString, which
older releases mapped to PyLong_AsLong and PyUnicode_FromString for
Python 3. pylibfdt/libfdt.i still uses them in two typemaps, so the
generated wrapper fails to compile ("implicit declaration of function
'PyInt_AsLong'"). Use the Python 3 functions directly.

Not specific to riscv32: any rebuild of dtc against swig 4.5.0 fails
the same way.
---
 main/dtc/APKBUILD | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main/dtc/APKBUILD b/main/dtc/APKBUILD
index 70cc231f64b..c4a38d6d7d5 100644
--- a/main/dtc/APKBUILD
+++ b/main/dtc/APKBUILD
@@ -25,6 +25,11 @@ prepare() {
 	default_prepare
 	sed -i s:-Werror::g "$builddir"/Makefile
 	sed -i "s|@VERSION@|$pkgver|" setup.py
+	# SWIG 4.5 no longer maps these Python 2 names to Python 3
+	# functions, and pylibfdt's typemaps still use them
+	sed -i -e 's/PyInt_AsLong/PyLong_AsLong/' \
+		-e 's/PyString_FromString/PyUnicode_FromString/' \
+		pylibfdt/libfdt.i
 }
 
 build() {
-- 
2.43.0

